hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19024","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jaafar, haddathana Shuba from al-Hakam who said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla narrating from a man from among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Goods brought for sale are not to be met on the way, and a townsman is not to sell for a Bedouin, and whoever buys a ewe with milk withheld, or a she-camel - Shuba said: He only said she-camel once - then he has the later of the two considerations when he milks it: if he returns it, he returns with it a saa of food. Al-Hakam said: Or he said: a saa of dates."
"19025","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Shuba, haddathana al-Hakam who said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla from a man from among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade unripe dates with ripe dates, and raisins with dates."
"19026","Haddathana Waki and Muhammad ibn Jaafar, both said: Thana Shuba from al-Hakam from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla - Ibn Jaafar said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla - from a man from among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not meet the riders. Ibn Jaafar said: Goods are not to be met, and a townsman is not to sell for a Bedouin, and whoever buys an animal with milk withheld, then he has therein the later of the two considerations - and Ibn Jaafar said: one of the two considerations: if he returns it, he returns with it a saa of food or a saa of dates."
"19027","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi from Sufyan from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla who said: Haddathani a man from among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cupping and continuous fasting, and did not prohibit them out of sparing his companions. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, you fast continuously till the sahar. He said: Though I fast continuously till the sahar, my Lord feeds me and gives me drink."
"19028","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, haddathana Sufyan from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abis from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from a man from among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cupping for the fasting one and continuous fasting, and did not prohibit them upon any of his companions. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you fast continuously till the sahar. He said: I fast continuously till the sahar, and my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, feeds me and gives me drink."
"19029","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi who said: Thana Sufyan from Mansur from Ribi ibn Hirash from some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: People woke upon the completion of thirty days, then two Bedouins came and testified that they had sighted it yesterday evening. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that they break fast."
"19030","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman from Sufyan from Mansur from Ribi ibn Hirash from some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede the month until you complete the count or see the crescent, and fast, and do not break fast until you complete the count or they see the crescent."
"19031","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jaafar, haddathana Shuba from al-Hakam who said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla narrating from a man from among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade unripe dates with ripe dates, and ripe dates with raisins."
